able with guessed ones.\\\\n\\\\nDELIVERABLES (absolute paths — create exactly these files, nothing else)\\\\n1. /home/sudhanshunaik/Projects/gpu-website-data/gpus.json\\\\n   A JSON array of GPU records. Every record MUST use exactly these keys:\\\\n   name, vendor, segment, architecture, launchYear, processNode, vramGB, memoryType,\\\\n   busWidthBits, bandwidthGBs, tdpW, msrpUSD (number or null), fp32TFLOPS (number or null),\\\\n   aiTops (number or null, dense/INT8 or FP8 — state which in \\\\\\\"aiTopsUnit\\\\\\\"),\\\\n   shaderCores (number or null), tensorCores (number or null), rtCores (number or null),\\\\n   sources (array of URL strings), confidence (\\\\\\\"high\\\\\\\" | \\\\\\\"medium\\\\\\\"), notes (string, may be \\\\\\\"\\\\\\\")\\\\n2. /home/sudhanshunaik/Projects/gpu-website-data/facts.md\\\\n   Markdown. Sections: \\\\\\\"Spec table\\\\\\\" (one row per GPU), \\\\\\\"Key facts\\\\\\\" (10-15 bullet claims a website would make, each with the source URL inline), \\\\\\\"Common myths / things people get wrong\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Numbers I could NOT verify\\\\\\\".\\\\n\\\\nREQUIRED COVERAGE — 12 to 16 GPUs, balanced across these buckets\\\\n- NVIDIA consumer (GeForce): RTX 5090, RTX 5080, RTX 5070, RTX 4090, RTX 4080 SUPER\\\\n- NVIDIA datacenter: H100 SXM5, H200 SXM, B200, A100 80GB SXM\\\\n- AMD: Radeon RX 9070 XT, Radeon RX 7900 XTX, Instinct MI300X\\\\n- Intel: Arc B580, Arc A770\\\\n\\\\nCONSTRAINTS\\\\n- Prefer primary sources: NVIDIA/AMD/Intel official product or datasheet pages, TechPowerUp GPU database, official press releases. Cite a URL for every row.\\\\n- Where a figure is vendor-claimed vs independently measured, say so in \\\\\\\"notes\\\\\\\".\\\\n- If you cannot verify a number, put null and say so in facts.md — do NOT invent or extrapolate a value. Do not interpolate bandwidth from bus width; cite it.\\\\n- Also record in facts.md, with sources: (a) the CPU-vs-GPU architectural difference in one paragraph, (b) why tensor cores exist