\n151|\\n152|## 3. Defects found by browser testing, and fixed\\n153|\\n154|1. **Success message was invisible (real bug, in `main.js`).** My `reset` listener cleared the status region, and `form.reset()` ran right after `setStatus(success)`, so the success confirmation was wiped within the same task. Fix: removed the now-purposeless reset listener and reset the fields *before* announcing. Re-verified: `state: success`, message still present 2 seconds later, fields cleared, URL unchanged.\\n155|2. **Two link groups were below the WCAG 2.5.8 target minimum.** Footer links measured `41x17` and contact-list links `19px` tall — not inline in a sentence, so no exemption applied. Fix: `display:inline-block` + block padding on `.footer-links a` and `.contact-list a`. Re-measured: `41x36` and `38px`. Nav links are `312x50`, the toggle `96x45`, buttons and inputs `51px` tall.\\n156|3. **A 404 on every page load.** Chrome's automatic `/favicon.ico` probe had no file to serve; adding a favicon file was forbidden by the file list, so I inlined one as a data-URI `<link rel=\\\"icon\\\">` in each page's `<head>`. Now the only requests a page makes are `style.css` and `main.js`.\\n157|\\n158|## 4. What I could not verify (and other caveats)\\n159|\\n160|- **Screen-reader output is unverified.** No screen reader exists here. A11y claims rest on markup, the computed Tab order and focus outlines, measured contrast, and live region attributes — not on hearing NVDA/VoiceOver.\\n161|- **Chrome only.** No Firefox or Safari. `:focus-visible`, `backdrop`-free CSS and the SVG favicon are the only mildly version-sensitive bits.\\n162|- **The horse emoji (🐴) in the titles** is added by the browser automation layer, not by me: `document.title` as read through the tool returns `\\\"🐴 Alex Rivera — Software Developer\\\"`, while the files on disk contain `<title>Alex Rivera — Software Developer</title>` (grep over all 5 files shows plain titles, no emoji).\\n163|- **Enter-key activation of the hamburger is unverified.** My synthetic CDP `Enter` generated 0 click events (a harness artifact), so I verified keyboard operability with `Space` (1 click → menu open) and the Tab/Escape path. I believe physical Enter behaves normally on a `<button>` but did not observe it here.\\n164|- Chrome's native validation bubbles and my inline error summary both appear on an invalid submit; I verified the summary and `aria-invalid`, not the bubble's presentation.\\n165|- The `mailto:` and three social links were not clicked (they would leave the page). They are anchors only — nothing is fetched; the only other URL-like strings in the site are two `example.com` URLs inside the sample post's `<pre><code>` block.\\n166|- Files touched outside the site folder: only my throwaway checker at `/home/sudhanshunaik/.hermes/profiles/frontend/cache/scratch/check_site.py` and the screenshots in the manager scratch path you specified. Nothing in your repos was modified.\\n167|- Two early screenshot attempts hit transient CDP IPC timeouts; every screenshot above was retaken successfully afterwards and all of them postdate the final edits.\", \"total_lines\": 167, \"file_size\": 13451, \"truncated\": false, \"is_binary\": false, \"is_image\": false, \"not_found\": false}", "tool_call_id": "call_00_oow3k5mMBukFzNU3UIsY6243", "tool_calls": null, "tool_name": "read_file", "effect_disposition": null, "timestamp": 1790788765.1239352, "token_count": null, "finish_reason": null, "reasoning": null, "reasoning_content": null, "reasoning_details": null, "codex_reasoning_items": null, "codex_message_items": null, "platform_message_id": null, "observed": 0, "active": 1, "compacted": 0, "api_content": null, "display_kind": null, "display_metadata": null, "message_uid": "5548585759a64cdab65c055539460186", "absorbed_message_uids": null, "tool_call_uids": null, "tool_call_uid": "698916e6220b4b45889fc438f67ac53d"}, {"id": 185, "session_id": "20260930_223741_8466aa", "role": "tool", "content": "{\"total_coun