nshunaik      36 Sep 24 18:03 models_dev_cache.etag\\n-rw-r--r--. 1 sudhanshunaik sudhanshunaik 4924700 Sep 24 18:03 models_dev_cache.json\\ndrwxr-xr-x. 1 sudhanshunaik sudhanshunaik      98 Sep 24 17:06 node\\ndrwx------. 1 sudhanshunaik sudhanshunaik       0 Sep 24 17:10 pairing\\ndrwxr-xr-x. 1 sudhanshunaik sudhanshunaik      14 Sep 24 19:39 platforms\\ndrwxr-xr-x. 1 sudhanshunaik sudhanshunaik       0 Sep 24 19:38 plugins\\n-rw-r--r--. 1 sudhanshunaik sudhanshunaik       2 Sep 24 19:49 processes.json\\ndrwxr-xr-x. 1 sudhanshunaik sudhanshunaik      96 Sep 30 20:38 profiles\\n-rw-r--r--. 1 sudhanshunaik sudhanshunaik     313 Sep 24 21:02 profile.yaml\\n-rw-r--r--. 1 sudhanshunaik sudhanshunaik   45056 Sep 24 19:29 projects.db\\n-rw-r--r--. 1 sudhanshunaik sudhanshunaik     114 Sep 24 21:02 provider_models_cache.json\\n===MANAGER profile.yaml===\\ndescription: Manager / orchestrator. Decomposes incoming work and dispatches it to\\n  specialist agents (researcher, backend, frontend, devops, reviewer) via 'hermes\\n  -p <agent> chat -q', then verifies and integrates their results. Answers trivial\\n  asks directly without fan-out.\\ndescription_auto: false\", \"exit_code\": 0, \"error\": null}", "tool_call_id": "call_00_os5o3syDg7zKlgGKxOY27936", "tool_calls": null, "tool_name": "terminal", "effect_disposition": null, "timestamp": 1790783474.9909265, "token_count": null, "finish_reason": null, "reasoning": null, "reasoning_content": null, "reasoning_details": null, "codex_reasoning_items": null, "codex_message_items": null, "platform_message_id": null, "observed": 0, "active": 1, "compacted": 0, "api_content": null, "display_kind": null, "display_metadata": null, "message_uid": "6aab4d68b54a3e6b0b4ba472998b394d", "absorbed_message_uids": null, "tool_call_uids": null, "tool_call_uid": null}, {"id": 46, "session_id": "20260930_212056_7bcb3d", "role": "tool", "content": "{\"success\": true, \"name\": \"agent-fleet-orchestration\", \"description\": \"Build a manager agent that dispatches to specialist agents.\", \"tags\": [\"multi-agent\", \"orchestration\", \"profiles\", \"bot-mode\", \"kanban\", \"delegation\", \"fleet\"], \"related_skills\": [\"hermes-agent\"], \"content\": \"---\\nname: agent-fleet-orchestration\\ndescription: \\\"Build a manager agent that dispatches to specialist agents.\\\"\\nversion: 1.0.0\\nauthor: Hermes Agent\\nlicense: MIT\\nplatforms: [linux, macos, windows]\\nmetadata:\\n  hermes:\\n    tags: [multi-agent, orchestration, profiles, bot-mode, kanban, delegation, fleet]\\n    related_skills: [hermes-agent]\\n---\\n\\n# Agent Fleet Orchestration\\n\\nBuild a **manager agent** that decomposes work and dispatches to **specialist agents**, all as Hermes profiles.\\n\\n## When to Use\\n\\n- The user wants a \\\"manager agent\\\", \\\"orchestrator\\\", \\\"team lead\\\", or \\\"agent that manages other agents\\\".\\n- The user wants named specialists (researcher, coder, analyst, writer) that keep their own persona, memory, and skills.\\n- An existing multi-agent setup needs a routing protocol, an evidence contract, or a dispatch loop that actually works headless.\\n\\nDo **not** use this for one-off parallel subtasks inside a single conversation — that is plain `delegate_task`.\\n\\n## The primitive: a specialist is a profile\\n\\nThere is no separate \\\"subagent\\\" object to invent. A specialist agent **is** a Hermes profile — its own `config.yaml`, `.env`, `SOUL.md`, skills, memory, and sessions under `~/.hermes/profiles/<name>/`.\\n\\nThat gives three coordinated layers, all over one primitive:\\n\\n| Layer | What it is | Use when |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **Profiles + shell dispatch** | `hermes -p <agent> chat -q \\\"<brief>\\\"` | Manager needs a real specialist persona, memory, and skills. Works headless. **Default choice.** |\\n| **Bot Mode** (desktop) | Named Bots roster, group chats, bot-to-bot DMs | Humans watching agents collaborate. Desktop-only UI. |\\n| **Kanban** | Durable SQLite task board, dispatcher routes by `profile.yaml` description | Long-running multi-profile work that must survive restarts. |\\n\\n## Build a fleet\\n\\n### 1. Create profiles with working credentials\\n\\n```bash\\nhermes profile create <agent> --clone --description \\\"<role the router can act on>\\\"\\n```\\n\\n- `--clone` copies `config.yaml`, `.env` (API keys), `SOUL.md`, skills, and memories — **without it the specialist has no credentials and cannot run.**\\n- `--description` is read by the **kanban decomposer** to route by role instead of by name. Write it as a capability statement, not a job title.\\n- Sets up a shell alias at `~/.local/bin/<agent>`, so `chief` alone launches that agent.\\n\\n### 2. Overwrite each SOUL.md with a role card\\n\\n`--clone` copies the parent's SOUL verbatim; replace it per agent. A role card needs:\\n\\n- **Lane** — what it owns, stated concretely\\n- **Anti-lane** — what it must hand back rather than half-do (`\\\"if it's really a build task, say so and hand it back\\\"`)\\n- **Output contract** — the exact shape of a good return, including a demand for evidence\\n- **Refusal rule** — the failure mode you most want prevented\\n\\nThe **manager's** card additionally carries the routing table and the dispatch protocol below.\\n\\n### 3. The dispatch protocol (manager's SOUL)\\n\\n```bash\\nhermes -p <agent> chat -q \\\"<complete, self-contained brief>\\\"\\n```\\n\\nCritical: **the specialist cannot see the manager's conversation.** A brief must stand alone — goal, deliverable format, absolute paths for inputs, constraints, and a demand for evidence (command output, source URL, computed numbers) rather than statements of intent.\\n\\nFan-out loop: **decompose → dispatch (independent briefs in parallel) → aggregate → verify → deliver one integrated answer.**\\n\\n### 4. Verify end to end — do not skip\\n\\n```bash\\nhermes -p <specialist> chat -q \\\"In two lines: your name, your lane, one thing you refuse.\\\"\\n```\\n\\nProves the persona loaded. Then prove the **dispatch loop** with a real task requiring a specialist, and confirm the manager returned an integrated answer with evidence — not a plausible summary.\\n\\n## Pitfalls\\n\\n- **No `--clone` = broken agent.** The profile will look created but fail on first run with no credentials.\\n- **Cloning copies the parent SOUL.** If you forget to overwrite it, every \\\"specialist\\\" answers as the generic parent agent — the fleet is cosmetic.\\n- **Ask for evidence, not intent.** A specialist self-report (`\\\"done\\\"`, `\\\"uploaded\\\"`) is not proof. For external side effects, require a handle — URL, commit SHA, absolute path — and check it from the manager.\\n- **Over-delegation is a failure mode.** Encode explicitly in the manager SOUL that a trivial ask gets a direct answer; fan-out is only for work that genuinely splits.\\n- **`hermes profile describe --all` requires `--auto`.** To read a single description, pass the name.\\n- **Bot Mode is desktop-only.** Profiles built from the CLI appear in the Bots tab automatically; group chats and bot-to-bot DMs have no CLI equivalent.\\n- **Local model trees are shared** when cloning from the default profile — `models/`, `runtimes/`, `node/` are not duplicated per profile.\\n- **Skill descriptions are capped at 60 chars** in the system-prompt index. A longer one aborts the create; keep it to one short sentence and put detail in the body.\\n- **A specialist will report an environment as \\\"incapable\\\" without trying to install anything.** Patching its SOUL with the concrete fallback fixes it permanently. For Python: `uv run --with <pkg> python -m pytest` installs a missing tool for one command with no project changes. Validate the fleet by asserting its environment claims yourself — a plausible-sounding \\\"the sandbox would not permit it\\\" is exactly the kind of unverified self-report a manager must check.\\n- **`hermes profile delete` can leave pending identity.** If it warns that session/routing identity settlement is pending, run `hermes profile purge-identity <name>` or the name stays half-reserved.\\n- **Deleting a profile does not always remove its shell alias.** Verify `~/.local/bin/<old-name>` is gone after a roster change, or the old agent stays invocable by name.\\n\\n## Adding a specialist later\\n\\nSame two steps: `hermes profile create <name> --clone --description \\\"...\\\"`, then write its `SOUL.md` and add a row to the manager's routing table. No restart, no registry.\\n\", \"path\": \"autonomous-ai-agents/agent-fleet-orchestration/SKILL.md\", \"skill_dir\": \"/home/sudhanshunaik/.hermes/profiles/manager/skills/autonomous-ai-agents/agent-fleet-orchestration\", \"org_provenance\": null, \"linked_files\": null, \"usage_hint\": null, \"required_environment_variables\": [], \"required_commands\": [], \"missing_required_environment_variables\": [], \"missing_credential_files\": [], \"missing_required_commands\": [], \"setup_needed\": false, \"setup_skipped\": false, \"readiness_status\": \"available\", \"_source_path\": \"/home/sudhanshunaik/.hermes/profiles/manager/skills/autonomous-ai-agents/agent-fleet-orchestration/SKILL.md\", \"metadata\": {\"hermes\": {\"tags\": [\"multi-agent\", \"orchestration\", \"profiles\", \"bot-mode\", \"kanban\", \"delegation\", \"fleet\"], \"related_skills\": [\"hermes-agent\"]}}}", "tool_call_id": "call_01_Qe2m72mArEkDUTDB4htW3107", "tool_calls": null, "tool_name": "skill_view", "effect_disposition": null, "timestamp": 1790783475.0297372, "token_count": null, "finish_reason": null, "reasoning": null, "reasoning_content": null, "reasoning_details": null, "codex_reasoning_items": null, "codex_message_items": null, "platform_message_id": null, "observed": 0, "active": 1, "compacted": 0, "api_content": null, "display_kind": null, "display_metadata": null, "message_uid": "61b8378ad405d641ed820eb99206e95f", "absorbed_message_uids": null, "tool_call_uids": null, "tool_call_uid": null}, {"id": 47, "session_id": "20260930_2120